 concise but complete, in Russian. Present blocker table with confidence markers, fix approach, VM protocol, and open decisions (C17 strict vs gnu17; strtok replacement choice). Ask for approval / decisions via plan presentation.\n\nActually, per instructions I can ask clarifying questions. The main decision: which fix approach for geometry.c and M_PI. Let me ask that as a question, plus whether to also fix gen_cloud includes. And confirm g++-14 install acceptable.\n\nLet me formulate the plan and a question with options.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the strtok approach once more. The current code:\n```c\nchar* copy = malloc(strlen(str) + 1);\nstrcpy_s(copy, strlen(str) + 1, str);\nchar* next_token = NULL;\nchar* pch = strtok_s(copy, \" \\t\\n\\r\", &next_token);\nint i = 0;\ndouble d[3];\nwhile (pch != NULL && i < 3) {\n    char* end_ptr = NULL;\n    d[i] = strtod(pch, &end_ptr);\n    if (*end_ptr != '\\0') { free(copy); return 2; }\n    pch = strtok_s(NULL, \" \\t\\n\\r\", &next_token);\n    ++i;\n}\nif (i != 3 || pch != NULL) { free(copy); return 1; }\n```\nNote: `i != 3 || pch != NULL` — after the loop, pch is the 4th token or NULL. If fewer than 3 tokens, pch==NULL and i<3 → return 1 (мало данных). If exactly 3 and no 4th → pch NULL, i==3 → ok. If extra tokens → i==3, pch non-NULL → return 1. OK.\n\nWait, there's a subtlety: if input has e.g. \"1 2 3.14abc\" → strtod parses 3.14, end_ptr at 'a', *end_ptr != '\\0' → return 2 (нечисловые данные). Good. If \"1 2\" → 2 tokens, pch NULL, i==2 → return 1. Good.\n\nStandard-C replacement with strspn/strtod:\n```c\nchar* copy = malloc(strlen(str) + 1);\nstrcpy(copy, str);   // or memcpy\nchar* p = copy;\nint i = 0;\ndouble d[3];\nwhile (i < 3) {\n    p += strspn(p, \" \\t\\n\\r\");\n    if (*p == '\\0') break;               // конец строки раньше времени → мало данных\n    char* end_ptr;\n    d[i] = strtod(p, &end_ptr);\n    if (end_ptr == p) { free(copy); return 2; }   // strtod ничего не распознал\n    if (*end_ptr != '\\0' && strchr(\" \\t\\n\\r\", *end_ptr) == NULL) { free(copy); return 2; }  // хвост-мусор\n    p = end_ptr;\n    ++i;\n}\nif (i != 3) { free(copy); return 1; }\np += strspn(p, \" \\t\\n\\r\");\nif (*p != '\\0') { free(copy); return 1; }   // лишние данные\n```\nHmm wait, need to double-check the \"too many\" case: after 3 tokens, skip spaces; if more chars → return 1. And the \"too few\" case: i<3 after loop → return 1. Also `end_ptr == p` catches \"abc\" (strtod returns 0, end=start) → нечисловые → 2. And \"1 2 xyz\": token2 \"2\" ok; token3 \"xyz\": end==p → 2. Good. \"1 2 3 4\": after 3, p skips spaces, *p='4' → return 1 (мало... rather \"лишние данные\" → code 1 = мало данных? In current code extra tokens → return 1 too (мало данных message?). Hmm, code 1 is \"мало данных\" but used for extra too. That's existing behavior; keep code semantics identical (1 = структура неверна, message may say \"мало данных X Y Z\" — existing behavior). I'll keep the codes exactly as-is to not change behavior. Actually messages differ: t3/t4 print \"Ожидается X Y Z, получено: ...\" for code 1 — and \"нечисловые данные\" for code 2. Keep same mapping.\n\nThis rewrite is standard C17, no _GNU_SOURCE, no strtok_s, no strcpy_s. Compiles identically on MSVC and Linux. Good recommendation.\n\nAlternatively keep strtok_s under #ifdef and strtok_r on Linux with -std=c17 + `#define _DEFAULT_SOURCE` at top. That's also fine and less code churn. But manual tokenizer avoids feature macros entirely and is a good C exercise. I'll present both, recommend manual.\n\nFor M_PI: fallback `#ifndef M_PI #define M_PI 3.14159265358979323846 #endif` — minimal, keep `-std=c17` both platforms. Good.\n\nFor includes: change `..\\common\\` → `../common/` in t2/t3/t4 mains (C & C++) and gen_cloud.\n\nAlright. Also potential: `#include <print>` in tests and mains — GCC 14 required; will verify version on VM.\n\nNow write plan. Keep it as the plan presented to the user. Since plan mode is active, I present plan and ask the decision question.\n\nOne more check — does the Makefile's Linux CXXFLAGS include anything MSVC-like? CXXFLAGS := $(CXXSTD) $(WARN) $(CONFIG_FLAGS) → `-std=c++23 -Wall -Wextra -O0 -g -fsanitize=address`. Fine.\n\nAlso `format-check` runs `clang-format --dry-run -Werror` on CP1251 files — clang-format may emit \"unable to parse\" or encoding errors? clang-format reads as bytes; invalid UTF-8 in comments/strings is passed through. Version differences could cause reformatting flags. Risk noted.\n\nAlso, the `test` target's first prerequisite is `format-check` → if clang-format missing, `make test` fails instantly. So install clang-format on VM, or for quick iteration use `make test` after installing. I'll include install step.\n\nAlso, I realize I should double-check: does the Makefile reference `$(GREP)` anywhere? Earlier grep found no usage of GREP in recipes. GREP variable unused now (was used with findstr before check.exe). Fine, harmless dead variable. Not a blocker. (Note: could be removed but not necessary.)\n\nNow, plan presentation. I'll be concise but complete. Provide the decision question at the end.\n\nActually the instructions: \"Ask the user clarifying questions or ask for their opinion when weighing tradeoffs.\" I'll present the plan and ask the strtok/M_PI approach question via the question tool.\n\nLet me draft the plan text in Russian, concise.",
